    "end": "Close enough.",
    "caption": "Wren's cup has been going cold since Monday.\n\nWhisk spins so fast that a day lasts six minutes. A year is over in a day and a half, so birthdays are relentless, lunch is largely theoretical and every calendar is a flipbook. Wren has twins, a kettle and one small ambition. The twins have other plans, and very good timing.\n\nI tried keeping a diary. By the time I'd written the date, it was wrong.\n\n(On Earth, the day gets about 1.8 thousandths of a second longer every century, as the tides drag on us. It won't help.)\n\nWhen did you last finish a hot drink?"
  },
